.TH SDL_UnloadObject 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_UnloadObject \- Unload a shared object from memory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_loadso.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_UnloadObject(SDL_SharedObject *handle);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note that any pointers from this object looked up through
.BR SDL_LoadFunction ()
will no longer be valid\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I handle
a valid shared object handle returned by
.BR SDL_LoadObject ()\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_LoadObject (3)
